  "body": "When it comes to favicons, the spec currently reads:\r\n\r\n> If there are multiple equally appropriate icons, user agents must use the last one declared in [tree order](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order) at the time that the user agent collected the list of icons.\r\n\r\nBut what about icon filetypes (such as `.ico`) that can have multiple icons embedded? Which embedded icon should the browser pick? The first? The last? The one with the most colored pixels (😜)?\r\n\r\nAs reported on https://alvaromontoro.com/blog/67996/the-mystery-of-the-changing-favicon, not all browsers behave in the same way. Currently, Chrome and Safari will choose the first icon it finds, whereas Firefox will pick the last one.",
